  "id": "cmp",
  "term": "CMP",
  "definition": "CMP usually refers to the Conway-Maxwell-Poisson regression model, a statistical method for count data. It is used when the spread of counts may be either lower or higher than expected under a standard Poisson model, making it a more flexible way to study relationships involving counts.",
